    "needsReview": [
      "The link received (1391:12671) is Checkbox Group, not Checkbox. This contract is for the Checkbox that group uses (837:25737, 216 variants). The group (up to 6 checkboxes vertically, gap spacing.3 in size 3) has no contract.",
      "The Checkbox Group description in Figma says \"radio buttons\": it is text copied from RadioGroup.",
      "Default values are marked with ✦ (\"surface ✦\", \"2 ✦\", \"unchecked ✦\", \"default ✦\"). The component set's default is `classic`.",
      "Indicator color (check and dash) read only in variant surface, without highContrast, default state: accent-contrast (check) and accent-alpha.11 (dash). It could not be read in the other combinations: the indicator color remains unverified.",
      "Tokens read in size 2. Sizes 1 and 3: only box, radius, gap and text style. In size 1 the check was not measured.",
      "highContrast only changes the checked background in classic and surface (accent.12); in soft it changes no colors, only opacity.",
      "opacity on hover/active (0.88, 0.82, 0.92) is hardcoded in Figma, with no variable. It is the only case where the contract uses opacity; disabled never does.",
      "disabled uses the same look for unchecked, checked and indeterminate (neutral-alpha.3 background, indicator not differentiated); the label text does not change color in disabled.",
      "classic adds shadows.shadow-1, also in disabled.",
      "No differentiated hover/active states for focus: the ring is a separate boolean.",
      "The box measures less than 24px: touch target below WCAG 2.5.8.",
      "No error state or required field in Figma."
    ]
  }
